    "text": "The Cyclone \u201cAkvan\u201d (pronounced: Akvan) over the Southeast Bay of Bengal and adjoining Southwest Bay of Bengal was centred near latitude 12.3\u00b0N and longitude 85.6\u00b0E (approximately 630 km from Trincomalee) at around 05.30 p.m. on 17th November 2026.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri,Bold",
      "Cambria"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      36.0,
      449.21,
      562.13,
      511.75
    ],
    "text": "The system is very likely to continue move slowly north-northwestwards and intensify further into a Severe Cyclonic Storm over the Westcentral Bay of Bengal around 05.30 a.m. on 18 th November 2026. Thereafter, it is likely to move northwestwards and intensify further into a very severe cyclonic storm around 05.30 p.m. of 19th November, 2026.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      36.0,
      530.59,
      561.53,
      559.51
    ],
    "text": "Continuing to move northwestward, it is likely to cross Andhra Pradesh & Yanam coasts between Nellore and Visakhapatnam, around 11.30 a.m. of 20th November, 2026 as a Very severe cyclonic storm.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri",
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      36.0,
      578.35,
      562.12,
      640.87
    ],
    "text": "Therefore, Naval and fishing communities are warned not to venture to the deep-sea areas bounded by 06N-19N and 80E-95E, and the sea areas off the coast extending from Kankasanthurai to Pottuvil via Trincomalee and Batticaloa, until further notice. Further, Naval and fishing communities operating in those sea areas are advised to move to safe areas.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri,Bold"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      36.0,
      653.74,
      562.12,
      682.54
    ],
    "text": "The naval and fishing communities, are requested to be attentive to the future forecasts and bulletins issued by the Department of Meteorology in this regard.",
    "fonts": [
      "Calibri"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      12.0
    ]
  },
